<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Godwin Friday</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">b. <a href="/years/1959">1959</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Godwin Friday is a Vincentian politician who became prime minister of Saint Vincent and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/grenadines">Grenadines</a> in November 2025. A lawyer and member of parliament for the Northern Grenadines since 2001, he became leader of the New Democratic Party in 2016. He led the party to victory in the general election of November 2025, ending 24 years of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/unity-labour-party">Unity Labour Party</a> government under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ralph-gonsalves">Ralph Gonsalves</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/godwin-friday.jpg" alt="Godwin Friday" width="320" height="426" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Lula Oficial · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Godwin_Friday_in_2026.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
